From: Agent
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: read the data FIFO one word per EMPTY check

SPL eMMC reads on H5 hang (no timeout, no error print) in the middle of a
CMD17 transfer, at a different block on each build. A hard bus lock is what
reading the FIFO register while it is empty causes, so do not trust the
FIFO level to read several words in a row: re-check the EMPTY flag before
every word.

---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -352,4 +352,7 @@
 		if (in_fifo > word_cnt - i)
 			in_fifo = word_cnt - i;
+		/* Level may overstate real FIFO content: one word per EMPTY check */
+		if (in_fifo > 1)
+			in_fifo = 1;
 		for (; in_fifo > 0; in_fifo--)
 			buff[i++] = readl_relaxed(&priv->reg->fifo);
